Usage: sdiff [OPTION] FILE1 FILE2

Side-by-side merge of differences between FILE1 and FILE2.
Display two files side by side, with differences marked.
Common lines are shown normally. Differences are marked with |,<,>.

OPTIONS:
  -o ARG                       output file
  -w ARG                       set output width
  -l                           print only the left column when lines are common
  -s, --suppress-common-lines  do not print common lines
  -B                           ignore changes whose lines are all blank
  -E                           ignore tab expansion
  -b                           ignore changes in amount of white space
  -W                           ignore all white space
      --help                   display this help and exit
  -V, --version                output version information and exit

EXIT STATUS:
  0  if OK,
  1  if minor problems,
  2  if serious trouble.

WinuxCmd is a Windows implementation of GNU CoreUtils for Linux-Windows developers and AI coding assistants.
